-- title:
--   Uniqueness of a valuation prolongation to the compositum with unramified constants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a discrete valuation ring $O$ that is a domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, a ring homomorphism $\iota_O\colon O\to\overline{\mathbf Q}$, a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with $\iota_O(a)\in A$ for all $a\in O$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ into a field $k$ of characteristic $p$. Let $F$ and $L$ be fields with ring homomorphisms $\theta_O\colon O\to L$ and $\theta_F\colon F\to L$ such that the subfield of $L$ generated by the union of their images is all of $L$, and let $\mathcal V,\mathcal W$ be valuation subrings of $L$. Assume: $p\neq 0$ in $L$ and $p$ lies in the nonunits of $\mathcal V$ and of $\mathcal W$; every nonzero $g\in\mathcal V$ has the form $p^n u$ with $n\in\mathbf N$ and $u$ a unit of $\mathcal V$ (i.e. $u,u^{-1}\in\mathcal V$); $\theta_O(O)\subseteq\mathcal V$ and $\theta_O(O)\subseteq\mathcal W$; the pullbacks agree, $\theta_F^{-1}(\mathcal V)=\theta_F^{-1}(\mathcal W)$; in $F$, the element $p$ is a nonunit of $\theta_F^{-1}(\mathcal V)$ and divides every such nonunit, in the sense that $f\cdot p^{-1}\in\theta_F^{-1}(\mathcal V)$ for every nonunit $f$; and there is a ring homomorphism $\rho\colon\mathcal W\to k((X))$ (Laurent series over $k$) whose zero set is exactly the nonunits of $\mathcal W$, which sends $\theta_O(a)$ to the constant series $\mathrm{red}(\iota_O(a))$ for all $a\in O$, and whose value on $\theta_F(f)$, for every $f\in F$ with $\theta_F(f)\in\mathcal W$, is the coefficientwise image under $\mathbf Z/p\to k$ of a Laurent series over $\mathbf Z/p$. Then $\mathcal V=\mathcal W$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness statement for the prolongation of a valuation of $F$ to the compositum $L$ generated by $F$ and the constants coming from $O$, in the shape needed to identify the two Gauss-type valuations on a function field of a modular curve: the hypotheses encode that $\mathcal V$ is $p$-adically generated by a uniformiser $p$, that $\mathcal V$ and $\mathcal W$ induce the same valuation on $F$, and that $\mathcal W$ reduces to Laurent series with $\mathbf F_p$-rational coefficients on $F$ and to constants on $O$. It is stated without reference to a level structure, and is used in the Deligne–Rapoport model package to show that the image of the stalk at the generic point under $\varphi$ lands in the integers of the relevant valuation.
